<?php
/**
 * Spartrak — the mobile filter drawer's header (Figma 864:20534).
 *
 * A close button on the inline-END edge and "فلترة" in --text/brand on the
 * inline-START edge, above the filter sidebar.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * WHY THIS IS A BLOCK IN sidebar.main AND NOT PART OF A DRAWER TEMPLATE
 * ===========================================================================
 * There is no drawer template. On mobile the EXISTING sidebar becomes the
 * drawer — CSS turns `.sidebar-main` into a fixed panel — so the chrome the
 * design puts around it has to be inside that same container, as siblings of
 * Mageplaza's filter block.
 *
 * Mounting it as a block `before="-"` in sidebar.main puts it first in the
 * DOM, which is exactly where the design puts it, with no `order` juggling
 * and nothing moved by script. Its counterpart, drawer-foot.phtml, mounts
 * `after="-"` for the same reason.
 *
 * Doing it this way rather than injecting the chrome with JS means the drawer
 * is complete in the server-rendered HTML: it cannot flash half-built, and it
 * is still correct if the widget never loads.
 *
 * DESKTOP: hidden in CSS. The sidebar is a plain column there and needs no
 * header — Figma's desktop sidebar (488:12197) has none.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Element\Template $block
 */
?>
<div class="spartrak-filter-drawer__head" aria-hidden="true">
    <?php /*
      DOM ORDER IS THE LAYOUT. The row is `justify-content: space-between`, so
      the FIRST child lands at the inline-start edge — the RIGHT in Arabic.
      Figma 864:20537 puts "فلترة" on the right and the close button on the
      left, so the TITLE COMES FIRST and the whole row mirrors itself for an
      LTR store with no second rule.

      `aria-hidden` on the wrapper and no heading semantics: the drawer's
      accessible name comes from the button that opens it and from the
      sidebar's own "خيارات التسوق" heading, which is real content. A second
      announced heading here would be noise.
    */ ?>
    <p class="spartrak-filter-drawer__title"><?= $block->escapeHtml(__('Filter')) ?></p>

    <button type="button"
            class="spartrak-filter-drawer__close"
            data-filter-drawer-close
            aria-label="<?= $block->escapeHtmlAttr(__('Close')) ?>">
        <span class="spartrak-filter-drawer__close-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </button>
</div>
